只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"dshell — a terminal-first AI workbench built as dsh plugins: one terminal timeline per session, cross-session pipes with a named buffer, SSH device sessions. | 终端优先的 AI 工作台（dsh 插件集）：一个会话一条终端时间线，跨会话管道委派与缓冲区文件共享，可把会话直接开到 SSH 设备上。","id":"gh:1362589427","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"Nexus-Terminal","slug":"Nexus-Aethra/Nexus-Terminal","topics":["dsh","dsh-bundle","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugin-market","dsh-plugins"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"dshell — a terminal-first AI workbench built as dsh plugins: one terminal timeline per session, cros"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"s-session pipes with a named buffer, SSH device sessions. | 终端优先的 AI 工作台（dsh 插件集）：一个会话一条终端时间线，跨会话管道委"},{"id":"p1s3","text":"派与缓冲区文件共享，可把会话直接开到 SSH 设备上。"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"**English** · 简体中文"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"# dshell — a terminal-first AI workbench"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"One session is one **terminal timeline**: you type in a real shell, and the AI keeps working on the\n"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"same screen. Every command you run and every turn the AI takes land in one column, in the order they"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"\nhappened. No chat bubbles."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"> The screenshots show the Chinese interface. dshell follows dsh's own language setting\n> (**Setting"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"s → General → Language**), so every dshell surface is available in English too."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"dshell is a set of plugins for **dsh** (DeepSeek Harness). It does not modify dsh's source: it plugs"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"\ninto dsh's documented extension points, so dsh stays upgradeable with upstream."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Contents"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"- How it fits together\n- What it is\n- What's new since 0.1.15\n- Getting started\n- A tour of the scre"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"en\n- Two modes: `$ shell` and `✦ agent`\n- The AI has a terminal of its own\n- Full-screen programs\n- "},{"id":"p8s3","text":"Input assists: Tab, ↑, →\n- **Cross-session collaboration: pipes and the buffer**\n- SSH device sessio"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"ns\n- Settings\n- The status card\n- Gesture cheat sheet\n- Three examples\n- Limits worth knowing\n- Docs"},{"id":"p8s5","text":" The status card\n- Gesture cheat sheet\n- Three examples\n- Limits worth knowing\n- Docs for developers"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## How it fits together"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"dshell is two layers: a **view** you look at, and a **host** that does the work. What you see is\nalw"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"ays a view of something else — which is why one column can hold your shell output and the AI's\nturns"},{"id":"p10s3","text":" at once, and why a session can be pointing at another machine while the window stays here."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Three bands, top to bottom:"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"- **The window** is the browser or the desktop app. It draws one column — your shell's output and\nth"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"e AI's turns, in the order they happened — and it sends what you type. It holds no state of its\nown:"},{"id":"p13s3","text":" everything on screen comes from the host over one websocket.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## What it is"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"| What you get | Details |"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"| A full-bleed terminal | One main shell per session, running real commands — full screen, colours, "},{"id":"p16s2","text":"cursor |\n| One merged timeline | Shell output and AI work interleave by time; each AI turn is a coll"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"apsible **task block** |\n| Two modes | `$ shell` makes Enter run a command, `✦ agent` makes Enter se"},{"id":"p16s4","text":"nd to the AI — the `$` / `✦` glyph in the input line is the mode, click it to flip |\n| The AI's own "},{"id":"p16s5","text":"shell | The AI gets a separate PTY, so it never blocks your foreground program and never steals your"},{"id":"p16s6","text":" terminal |\n| Cross-session work | Sessions form **pipes** to delegate tasks to each other and share"},{"id":"p16s7","text":" files by name (the **buffer**) — including across SSH devices |\n| Device sessions | Open a session "},{"id":"p16s8","text":"directly on a remote machine: commands, files and the visible terminal all run there |\n| WSL2 device"},{"id":"p16s9","text":"s | A WSL2 distribution on this Windows machine is a device row of its own — its own terminal, files"},{"id":"p16s10","text":" and agent session, with no credential to enter |\n| Context without retelling | Switching to `✦ agen"},{"id":"p16s11","text":"t` automatically carries your last few commands and their output to the AI |"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## What's new since 0.1.15"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"`0.1.17` is on npm as `latest`. It is the release that makes a terminal survive a session\nswitch, tu"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"rns a WSL2 distribution into a device row, and carries the port forwards that connect\na local port t"},{"id":"p18s3","text":"o a service on the device."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Its predecessor `0.1.16` changed one thing that matters at install time on its own: dshell no\nlonger"},{"id":"p19s2","text":" pins a single dsh version but names a **window** of them, so every `0.2.1` release —\n`0.2.1-rc.5`, "},{"id":"p19s3","text":"today's `latest`, included — installs without waiting for a dshell release."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"| | What changed | What you notice |"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"| **WSL2 distributions are devices** | A WSL2 distribution on this Windows machine is detected and o"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"ffered as a **built-in device row** of its own — open a terminal on it, browse its files, hand it to"},{"id":"p21s3","text":" the AI | There is **no credential to enter** (the distribution is its own credential) and **no port"},{"id":"p21s4","text":" forward** to ask for: WSL2 shares this machine's loopback, so its ports are already reachable here "},{"id":"p21s5","text":"|\n| **The 管理台** | dsh's Settings gains a **dshell** section — one page that gathers the whole suite'"},{"id":"p21s6","text":"s settings | **设备与凭据**, **WSL 发行版** and **终端与数据** as three cards on one page, instead of a configure"},{"id":"p21s7","text":" control per plugin row |\n| **A ConPTY repaint no longer blanks the terminal** | On Windows, a progr"},{"id":"p21s8","text":"am that repaints its whole screen after a resize — the ConPTY signature — left a **blank wall above "},{"id":"p21s9","text":"the prompt** | The region renders the rows that carry ink and cuts the dead frame around them, so th"},{"id":"p21s10","text":"e row count and the bytes agree again |\n| **A session switch keeps its prompt** | Switching to a ses"},{"id":"p21s11","text":"sion and back reset its readiness, so a live device session flashed the first-dial panel over a term"},{"id":"p21s12","text":"inal that was about to work | That the session reached a prompt is remembered for the page's life **"},{"id":"p21s13","text":"and across a reload**, and seeded while the rebind handshake runs |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"### What one delegation looks like"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Delegation is **asynchronous**. A busy peer simply queues the request, and the requester does not\nbl"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"ock: its turn ends, and it is woken up again when the answer comes back."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"The peer sees **only what you send it**: not your other files, not your other sessions. Tickets have"},{"id":"p25s2","text":" a\ndeadline; a watchdog settles an unanswered one as `已超时` and tells the requester, who can delegate"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"\nagain or carry on alone."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"### What the detail page shows"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"Clicking a pipe opens its detail page:"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"- **缓冲区** — a walkable tree with the same feel as the right sidebar's file browser (crumbs,\n`刷新`, ho"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"ver highlight); each row says where it came from and with which rights.\n- **进行中的请求 / 已结束** — every t"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"icket's state, direction, subject and full reply.\n- **生效中的授权** — the grants that are live right now,"},{"id":"p29s4","text":" and the real path each one maps."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"The screenshot above is a pipe **after** its task settled: the grants have already been reclaimed, s"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"o\nthe buffer is empty again. That is by design."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
